{% comment %}
  The three ways a customer can get film to the lab.

  Route 1 (prepaid label) is the one we sell, so it carries the accent border
  and a direct add-to-cart on the cheapest variant. The other two routes are
  given equal descriptive weight so customers who ship their own or drop off
  are not pushed toward a purchase they do not need.

  Turnaround times are deliberately not stated here. They live in the
  announcement bar, which is the single place the lab keeps current.

  Accepts:
    - show_heading {Boolean} Render the heading and intro above the options.
    - heading {String} Overrides the default heading. The home page introduces
      these same three routes to a visitor who has not yet decided to order, so
      it needs to lead with the question rather than the answer.
    - intro {String} Overrides the default supporting line.

      Both exist so a caller can retitle the block without wrapping it in its
      own container. A wrapper is what broke this on the home page once: the
      prose block caps at 72rem while the options grid below runs to 110rem, so
      the introduction ended up in a visibly narrower column than the cards it
      was introducing.
    - pack_link {String} Where the "How to pack your film" button points. The
      mail-in page passes its own in-page anchor so the button scrolls down to
      the packing section instead of reloading the page the customer is on.
      Defaults to the packing section on the mail-in page.

  Usage:
    {% render 'cfl-shipping-options' %}
    {% render 'cfl-shipping-options', pack_link: '#cfl-packing' %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign label_product = all_products['in-bound-label']
  assign label_variant = label_product.variants | sort: 'price' | first

  assign packing_url = pack_link
  unless packing_url
    assign packing_url = pages['mail-in'].url | append: '#cfl-packing'
  endunless
-%}

<div class="cfl-ship-options-wrapper">
  {%- if show_heading -%}
    <h2 class="cfl-section-heading">{{ heading | default: 'Getting your film to us' }}</h2>
    <p class="cfl-section-intro">
      {{- intro | default: 'Three ways to do it. Pick whichever suits you. Your order is processed the same either way.' -}}
    </p>
  {%- endif -%}

  <ul class="cfl-ship-options" role="list">
    {%- comment -%} Route 1: buy a prepaid label from us. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if label_product != blank and label_product.available -%}
      <li class="cfl-ship-option cfl-ship-option--featured">
        <span class="cfl-ship-option__tag">Easiest</span>
        <h3 class="cfl-ship-option__title">Buy a prepaid label</h3>
        <div class="cfl-ship-option__body">
          <p>
            Add a shipping label to your order and we'll email you a private link right after
            checkout. Fill in your address, pick USPS or UPS, and print the label, or wait for
            the copy we email you.
          </p>
          <p>
            {{ label_product.variants.size }} package sizes, from a padded mailer up to a
            large box.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="cfl-ship-option__action">
          {%- form 'product', label_product, id: 'cfl-label-quick-add', class: 'cfl-ship-option__form' -%}
            <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ label_variant.id }}">
            <button
              type="submit"
              name="add"
              class="button button--primary"
              {% unless label_variant.available %}
                disabled
              {% endunless %}
            >
              Add a {{ label_variant.title }} label — {{ label_variant.price | money }}
            </button>
          {%- endform -%}
          <p class="cfl-ship-option__note">
            Sending more than fits a {{ label_variant.title | downcase }}?
            <a href="{{ label_product.url }}">
              Compare all {{ label_product.variants.size }} sizes
            </a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%} Route 2: customer buys their own postage. {%- endcomment -%}
    <li class="cfl-ship-option">
      <h3 class="cfl-ship-option__title">Ship it yourself</h3>
      <div class="cfl-ship-option__body">
        <p>
          Already have postage sorted? Send your film to us with any carrier you like. Use a
          padded mailer or a small box — not a paper envelope — and hold on to your tracking
          number.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Coastal Film Lab</strong><br>
          1704 N Nebraska Ave<br>
          Tampa, FL 33602
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cfl-ship-option__action">
        <a href="{{ packing_url }}" class="button button--secondary">How to pack your film</a>
      </div>
    </li>

    {%- comment -%} Route 3: local drop-off. {%- endcomment -%}
    <li class="cfl-ship-option">
      <h3 class="cfl-ship-option__title">Drop it off</h3>
      <div class="cfl-ship-option__body">
        <p>
          In the Tampa Bay area? The counter is open Monday, Tuesday, Thursday and Friday
          10am–6pm, and Saturday 10am–3pm. Outside those hours use the drop box between our two
          front doors. There's a second one in the back parking lot. We develop film every day,
          including the days the shop is closed to walk-ins.
        </p>
        <p>No shipping to buy. Just include your name and order number.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cfl-ship-option__action">
        <a
          href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/L6UsTYjCe1A6vVocA"
          class="button button--secondary"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
        >
          Get directions
        </a>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p class="cfl-section-intro cfl-ship-options__footnote">
    Whichever route you pick, write your name and order number on a slip of paper and put it in
    with your film. Want your negatives back? Choose a return shipping option at checkout.
    That's separate from any label you buy to send film to us.
  </p>
</div>
